<title>GREECE: EU INVESTMENT BANK LENDS GREECE $254MLN FOR GAS NETWORK - PLATT'S.</title>
<headline>EU INVESTMENT BANK LENDS GREECE $254MLN FOR GAS NETWORK - PLATT'S.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank, the lending arm of the European Union, signed a new 60.6 billion drachma ($254 million) loan agreement with the Public Gas Corporation of Greece, Platt's said.</p>
<p>The loan will help finance the construction and operation of a high pressure transmission and distribution system for natural gas in Greece, the EIB said.</p>
<p>Construction work on this project began in 1990 and it is expected to begin operation in 1999, the bank added.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
